'''Amatista''' is the eighth planet from the star Aurelius, orbiting in the vast middle region of the system beyond the habitable zone planets [[Adonia]], [[Aztlán]], and [[Cíbola]]. It is a massive gas giant, the second largest in the system by mass, and is instantly recognizable by its deep, vibrant violet and indigo coloration.

While [[Quetzal]] dominates the inner system with its heat and proximity, Amatista rules the middle system with its cold majesty. It acts as the gravitational anchor for the outer planets. Its distinct purple hue is attributed to high concentrations of complex phosphines and hydrocarbons in its upper atmosphere, which absorb green and red light while reflecting blue and violet.

Amatista is also unique for its ring system. Unlike the bright, icy rings of [[Centinela]], Amatista's rings are composed of dark, carbon-rich dust and rock. These rings have a very low albedo, appearing like bands of soot against the planet's bright cloud tops. They cast broad, sharp shadows across the northern hemisphere, creating a stark visual contrast that changes with the planet's seasons.

==Physical characteristics==
===Atmosphere===
The atmosphere of Amatista is a turbulent envelope of hydrogen and helium. The upper cloud deck is dominated by ammonia ice and phosphine haze. The distinct purple color differentiates it from the brownish-orange of Quetzal or the beige of [[Alcázar]]. The atmosphere features zonal banding, with dark indigo belts alternating with lighter amethyst zones.

Storms on Amatista are long-lived and massive. The Great Violet Spot, a high-pressure anticyclonic storm similar to Jupiter's Great Red Spot, has been observed for centuries. It is large enough to engulf the entire planet of [[Adonia]]. Lightning strikes in the deep atmosphere are believed to be thousands of times more powerful than terrestrial lightning, converting methane into carbon soot which may rain down into the interior.

===Ring system===
Amatista is surrounded by the Carbon Rings, a massive system of dark debris. The rings are believed to be the remnants of a carbonaceous asteroid or a small moon that ventured past the Roche limit and was torn apart by tidal forces. Because the particles are so dark, the rings were not discovered until the invention of advanced telescopes on Adonia, appearing initially as a shadow rather than a structure.

==Orbit and rotation==
Amatista orbits Aurelius at an average distance of 5.40 AU, completing a revolution every 4,600 standard days (approximately 12.6 Adonian years). This distance places it well beyond the frost line, allowing volatile compounds to condense into the ices that make up its many moons.

The planet is a rapid rotator, spinning on its axis once every 10.2 hours. This rapid rotation causes the planet to be visibly oblate, bulging at the equator and flattening at the poles. It also drives the ferocious wind speeds in its atmosphere, which can exceed 500 m/s.

==Name and etymology==
The name Amatista is derived from the Insulonian word for Amethyst, the precious violet quartz. In ancient mythology, the gemstone was believed to protect its owner from intoxication and keep the mind clear, a trait attributed to the planet's steady, unblinking presence in the night sky compared to the wandering inner planets.

In Sanese astronomical nomenclature, the planet is known as Shiunsei (紫雲星), translating to the Purple Cloud Star. This name is considered an auspicious omen in Sanese culture, as purple clouds were often associated with the arrival of a deity or a great emperor.

